{"name":"Frisky","hex":"#ccdda1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"frisky","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Abounding in energy or playfulness.","Sexually aroused."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frisky"}],"entries":[{"title":"Meadows Frisky","blocks":[{"text":"Meadows Frisky is the name of a series of small British cars manufactured at the factory of Henry Meadows Ltd at Fallings Park in Wolverhampton between 1958 and 1961, during which time production was under the control of a number of companies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/FriskyLogo.svg/330px-FriskyLogo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meadows_Frisky","wikidata":"Q1465097"},{"title":"Frisky Tom","blocks":[{"text":"Frisky Tom is a 1981 action video game developed by Jorudan and published by Nichibutsu for arcades. It was released in Japan in September 1981 and North America in November 1981. In this game, the player assumes the role of a plumber, named Tom, who is tasked with protecting and maintaining a network of plumbing pipes that route water from a storage tank to a shower."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8e/Frisky_Tom_1981_Arcade_Flyer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frisky_Tom","wikidata":"Q1465103"},{"title":"Frisky (Tinie Tempah song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Frisky\" is a song by English rapper Tinie Tempah, crediting the song's producer Labrinth as its featured artist. The track was released in the United Kingdom on 7 June 2010 as the second single from the musician's debut studio album, Disc-Overy (2010). On the chart week ending 19 June 2010, \"Frisky\" debuted at number two on the UK Singles Chart behind \"Shout\" by Shout for England; in Scotland, it debuted at number one, becoming Tempah's second number-one single there."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0c/Tinie_Tempah_Frisky_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frisky_(Tinie_Tempah_song)","wikidata":"Q1990735"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/1957MeadowsBug.jpg/330px-1957MeadowsBug.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/1957MeadowsBug.jpg/330px-1957MeadowsBug.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"The Bug\" in 1957 with designer Gordon Bedson behind the wheel","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1957MeadowsBug.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/MeadowsFriskyGull_wing.jpg/330px-MeadowsFriskyGull_wing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/MeadowsFriskyGull_wing.jpg/330px-MeadowsFriskyGull_wing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Michelotti-designed Meadows Frisky at the 1957 Geneva Show","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMeadowsFriskyGull_wing.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Coupe1958showcar.jpg/330px-Coupe1958showcar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Coupe1958showcar.jpg/330px-Coupe1958showcar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The 1958 Frisky Coupe","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACoupe1958showcar.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/FriskyFamilyThree1959.jpg/330px-FriskyFamilyThree1959.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"